<title>MALAYSIA: Hock Hua shares surges on bonus plan.</title>
<headline>Hock Hua shares surges on bonus plan.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Malaysia's Hock Hua Bank Bhd surged in early trading following its proposal for a two-for-one bonus issue.</p>
<p>At 0144 GMT, the stock was up 1.60 ringgit or 16.00 percent to 11.60 ringgit on volume of 137,000 shares traded.  </p>
<p>The bank said on Thursday it planned to make a bonus issue of 263 million new shares, and a one-for-one rights issue priced at 2.25 ringgit.</p>
<p>Hock Hua foreign-shares rose 1.40 ringgit or 14.74 percent to 10.90 on volume of 52,000 shares traded.</p>
</text>
